      "message": "[error] Line 4730: 🔴 `merge()` still holds `callMutex_` via `lk1` when calling `requestTransportFallback()`, and `requestTransportFallback()` immediately takes `callMutex_` again. If `callMutex_` is non-recursive, this is a self-deadlock on conference join. Fix by either (a) moving the `requestTransportFallback()` call after the merge locks are released, or (b) splitting into a `requestTransportFallbackLocked()` variant that assumes the caller already holds the lock and does not relock.",
      "revId": "e56db50c7a61f4aca5b26d194fbd42dd19a04bee",
