      "message": "[warning] Line 1067: 🟡 The expected ICE component set is computed as `1..(attributes.size()*2)` when RTCP mux is disabled, but ICE component IDs in SDP candidates are per-media RTP/RTCP component identifiers (typically `1` and `2`), not globally incremented across m-lines. With audio+video this can wrongly expect `{1,2,3,4}` and fail on valid SDP. Fix by asserting `{1,2}` for non-mux (or validating components per m-line instead of one global set).",
